    "created_at": "2016-10-13T16:57:58Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-13T16:57:58Z",
    "body": "Very interesting. Other possibilities: autocomplete, autofocus. (I wonder why autofocus is nested under the \"Form submission\" section.)\n\nI guess those sections would move under 6.6 Editing. Their wording will need to be rejiggered to talk less about form controls, and more about whatever we end up calling editable controls per https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/1892. Some new examples would be good.\n\nAnd I guess all the element definitions that say that these attributes apply to only certain elements would need to remove that line, and they would need to move to the \"Global attributes\" section. Then the individual sections would need a conformance requirement saying that they are only used on editable controls.\n\nFirst step is deciding which attributes beyond inputmode we want to move, IMO.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
